menu "OCTO Radio"

    choice RADIO_OCTOPUS_QUALITY
        prompt "Main page octopus scene"
        default RADIO_OCTOPUS_QUALITY_FULL
        help
            How much work the animated octopus on the main page does per frame.

            Full draws every layer as designed. Lite keeps the same scene, the
            same animation and the same frame rate target, and spends less time
            per frame by shading each arm with 3 bands instead of 6 and placing
            them further apart. It differs from Full only in the smoothness of
            the arm shading. Choose Lite if Full does not reach a steady frame
            rate on the device, or if audio glitches while it runs.

            Off shows the plain water background with no octopus, for finding
            out whether the scene is the cause of a problem.

        config RADIO_OCTOPUS_QUALITY_FULL
            bool "Full"

        config RADIO_OCTOPUS_QUALITY_LITE
            bool "Lite"

        config RADIO_OCTOPUS_QUALITY_OFF
            bool "Off (water only)"

    endchoice

    config RADIO_OCTOPUS_FRAME_MS
        int "Octopus frame interval (ms)"
        range 33 250
        default 80
        help
            Time between octopus frames. 80 is about 12 frames per second. Raise
            it to leave more CPU for audio and Wi-Fi, lower it for smoother motion.

endmenu
